      "result": "I fixed two defects in `ledger.py` and updated `DOSSIER.md`. The supplied suite now passes (10 tests OK). It had 1 failure and 2 errors before the edits.\n\n**Acceptance example:** `decide(\"original\", 4000.00)` under BR-001/v1 gives `STANDARD_QUEUE`. After `activate(\"BR-001/v2\")`, the same retry returns `REPLAYED` with a record identical to the original. The row counts in `decisions` and `audit_events` don't change. A fresh ID with the same payload now gives `HUMAN_REVIEW`.\n\n**Corrections:**\n1. **Retry after a policy change.** `PolicyStore._decide` re-ran the outcome under the active policy when it found an existing key. That overwrote the stored decision, so a retry after activating v2 returned the wrong result. I removed that step, so the stored record comes back unchanged. This fixed the failing test.\n2. **Legacy migration.** `migrate_legacy` started with `raise NotImplementedError`, which made the rest of the function unreachable. I removed that line. The existing body already validates provenance, policy and outcome, runs in one transaction, and leaves `legacy_decisions` untouched. This fixed both migration test errors.\n\nI also ran a throwaway probe against a temporary database. It rejected `+1.00`, a trailing newline, a fullwidth digit, 13 integer digits and 3 fractional digits. It accepted `007.5`. Under `-I`, `-0` was accepted and routed to `REJECTED`. An explicit v2 under an old v1 ID raised `IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT`.\n\n**Limits:**\n- I tested only the one supplied legacy fixture shape. The migration failure paths (ambiguous policy, outcome mismatch, wrong schema) are checked by reading the code only.\n- I did not test concurrency or a crash mid-migration.\n- The task mentions \"three proposals\", but none were in the workspace, so I made no ACCEPT/REJECT/ASK ruling on them. The dossier says so; please supply them if you expect a ruling.\n- I found no conflict between the docs and no missing rule for this increment, so I didn't need to stop and ask.\n- Human acceptance is not given. I made no network calls and installed nothing.\n\nChanged files: `ledger.py` and `DOSSIER.md`. I used 5 tool commands in this run, out of the 40 allowed.",
